      <div type="clause" n="36">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 36</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="36" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="338" ed="#liebermann"/>And<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_36.lnote.oe.5"/> gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_36.lnote.oe.6-3"/> hwa mæne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="††" target="#IICn_36.lnote.oe.dagger2"/> að on haligdome swerige, ⁊ he oferstæled<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_36.lnote.oe.7-3"/> weorðe, þolige þæra handa oððe healfes weres; ⁊ þ<hi rend="italic">æt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_36.lnote.oe.5"/></hi> sy gemæne hlaforde ⁊ bisceope.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_36.lnote.oe.8-3"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="36" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="338" ed="#liebermann"/>Be mænan aðe. Gyf hwa mæne að on haligdome swerie, ⁊ he oferstǽled weorðe, ðolie ðara hánda oððe healfes weres; ⁊ ðæt sy gemæne hlaforde ⁊ bisceope.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="36" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="338" ed="#liebermann"/>And gif hwa mæne að on haligdome swerige, ⁊ he oferstaled geweorðe, þolige þara handa oððe healfes weres; ⁊<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_36.lnote.oe.2"/> sy gemæne hlaforde ⁊ biscope.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="36" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="339" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis falsum iuramentnm super sancta<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_36.lnote.oe.6-2"/> iurabit et conuictus inde fuerit, manum perdat uel<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_36.lnote.oe.7-2"/> dimidiam wéram; et hoc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_36.lnote.oe.8-2"/> commune sit domino<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_36.lnote.oe.9"/> et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_36.lnote.oe.10"/> episcopo.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="36" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="339" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis periurium fecerit super textum euangelil aut super reliquias sanctorum et uictus fuerit, quod iniuste iurauerit, careat manibus aut det dimidium prętii<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_36.lnote.oe.7-4"/> sui ipsius; et hoc diuidatur inter episcopum et dominum ipsius hominis.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="36" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="339" ed="#liebermann"/>Eṭ si quis mendacium super sacrato iurauerit et conuictus fuerit, amittat manum aut dimidiam redempcionem sui, quę communis sit domino et episcopo.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="36" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="194" ed="#robertson"/>Be mænan aðe. Gyf hwa mæne að on haligdome swerie ⁊ he oferstǽled weorðe, ðolie ðara hánda oððe healfes weres, ⁊ ðæt sy gemæne hlaforde ⁊ bisceope.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="274" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And gyf hwa mæne að on haligdome swerige, and he oferstæled weorðe, þolige þæra handa oððe healfes weres, and þæt sy gemæne hlaforde and bisceope.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="338" ed="#liebermann"/>(Vom Meineid. <hi rend="italic">B</hi>) Und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_36.lnote.de.1"/> wenn einer falschen Eid<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_36.lnote.de.2"/> auf die Reliquien<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_36.lnote.de.3"/> schwört und überführt wird, verliere er die [Schwur]hand<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_36.lnote.de.4"/> oder [sein] halbes Wergeld; und letzteres sei halb getheilt dem [Gerichts]herrn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_36.lnote.de.5"/> und [halb] dem Bischof.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(Of false oaths. B) And if anyone swears a false oath on relics and is convicted, let him lose the [swearing] hand or half [his] wergild; and let the latter be shared between the lord [of the court] and the bishop.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_36.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="195" ed="#robertson"/>Concerning perjury. If anyone swears a false oath on the relics and is convicted, he shall lose his hand<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_36.robnote.n.2"/> or half his wergeld which shall be divided between the lord and the bishop.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="467" ed="#whitelock"/>And if anyone swears a false oath on the relics, and is confuted, he is to forfeit his hands or half his wergild; and it is to be divided by the lord and the bishop.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="275" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And if anyone swears a false oath over the relics and is convicted, he shall either lose his hand or half his wergild, which is to be shared between king and bishop.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="338"><ref target="clause:IIAs_26">II As 26</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. II As. 26</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="359"><label>loose/partial source (in parentheses)</label> <ref target="clause:IIAs_26">II As 26</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 36-36:1: (II As 26)</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">G's ‘mæne’ for ‘mænne’. ‘þæt’ supplied in A. Liebermann compares II As 26.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 339, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">B adds rubric Be mænan aðe</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">And: omitted B</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_36.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">339</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-tum <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-tum Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_36.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">339</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Hk;</hi> que <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">so Hk; que Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_36.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">339</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ep. et do. sit <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ep. et do. sit Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_36.lnote.oe.6-2" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">339</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sacra <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sacra K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_36.lnote.oe.7-2" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">339</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">aut <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">aut K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_36.lnote.oe.8-2" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">339</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">omne <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">omne K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_36.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">339</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">suo <hi rend="italic">fügt zu RTHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">RTHk add suo</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_36.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">339</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_36.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">338</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_36.lnote.oe.6-3" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">338</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gif <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gif Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_36.lnote.oe.dagger2" n="††" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">338</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">statt</hi> mænne</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">instead of mænne</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_36.lnote.oe.7-3" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">338</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-staled geweorþe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-staled geweorþe Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_36.lnote.oe.8-3" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">338</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-cope <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-cope Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_36.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">338</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze</hi> þæt</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply þæt</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_36.lnote.oe.7-4" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">339</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd.</hi> prętium <hi rend="italic">H;</hi> pretium <hi rend="italic">Di</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to prętium H; pretium Di</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_36.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">207</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Benutzt durch Hn 11, 6</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Used by Hn 11, 6</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_36.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">207</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Meineid 13</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Meineid 13</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_36.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">207</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Zu Inst's Zusatz <hi rend="italic">vgl. Gl</hi> Eidesform 7a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">On Inst’s addition <hi rend="italic">cf. Gl</hi> Eidesform 7a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_36.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">207</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Hände’ Inst, Price-Thorpe, wie <hi rend="italic">o</hi>. 8, 1¹. Allein ¹/₂ Wergeld entspricht Einer Hand (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 9. 11a), und dies ist Strafe für Meineid in vielen German. Rechten</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘Hands’ Inst, Price-Thorpe, as <hi rend="italic">above</hi> 8, 1¹. But ¹/₂ wergild corresponds to one hand (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 9. 11a), and this is the penalty for perjury in many Germanic laws</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_36.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">207</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Also die staatliche Gewalt richtet und straft. Nur den Justizertrag überlässt sie zur Hälfte der Kirche, die durch Missbrauch ihrer Heiligtümer beleidigt war; <hi rend="italic">s. Gl</hi> Kirchenstaatsrecht 16</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Thus it is the authority of the state that judges and punishes. Only half of the judicial revenue does it leave to the Church, which had been offended by the misuse of its relics; <hi rend="italic">see Gl</hi> Kirchenstaatsrecht 16</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_36.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">356</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. II As. 26.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_36.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">356</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">ðara hánda</hi> here, as in cap. 8, 1, is to be taken as sing. in view of the alternative, cf. Af. 71 and note.</seg></note>
      </div>
